  "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/code-yeongyu/oh-my-openagent/tarball/v5.1.27",
  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/code-yeongyu/oh-my-openagent/zipball/v5.1.27",
  "body": "**omo runs on senpi 2026.10.10-9, which stops automatic turns from running without bound.** After one message from you, stream-rule nudges, goal continuations and other automatic follow-ups pause after 150 turns, or once 12 automatic turns in a minute do no work, and each stream rule corrects a message at most once. When it pauses, the session says so, and your next message picks it back up. Full engine notes: [senpi 2026.10.10-9](https://github.com/code-yeongyu/senpi/releases/tag/v2026.10.10-9). ([senpi#2967](https://github.com/code-yeongyu/senpi/issues/2967), [senpi#2969](https://github.com/code-yeongyu/senpi/pull/2969), [#9772](https://github.com/code-yeongyu/oh-my-openagent/pull/9772))\n\n**A required question can't be read as permission.** senpi's `ask_user_question` accepts `required: true` for a question that gates an action, such as an approval before an irreversible step: if it times out, is dismissed or can't be shown, the model is told not to take that action. ([senpi#2949](https://github.com/code-yeongyu/senpi/issues/2949), [senpi#2959](https://github.com/code-yeongyu/senpi/pull/2959))\n\n**The configuration guide documents the Anthropic 1-hour prompt cache and the cache keep-alive.** ([#9770](https://github.com/code-yeongyu/oh-my-openagent/issues/9770), [#9771](https://github.com/code-yeongyu/oh-my-openagent/pull/9771))\n\n### Fixed\n\n**Memory locks stop churning on machines with many sessions.** A session waiting on a memory lock no longer republishes a recovery lock on every retry: it reads first, and lock polls back off with jitter instead of a fixed 25 ms. Locks and candidate files left by processes that died are reclaimed, so the lock directory stops growing. ([#9749](https://github.com/code-yeongyu/oh-my-openagent/issues/9749), [#9750](https://github.com/code-yeongyu/oh-my-openagent/pull/9750))\n\n**Single-turn answers no longer carry the progress-ledger block.** Hephaestus and Sisyphus keep the Now/Next ledger for multi-step work tracked in todos; a request finished in one turn gets a plain answer, without lines such as `Next: none`. Thanks to @cynkai. ([#9616](https://github.com/code-yeongyu/oh-my-openagent/issues/9616), [#9676](https://github.com/code-yeongyu/oh-my-openagent/pull/9676))\n\n**A provider that sets its own `anthropic-beta` header keeps the betas a request needs**, so Claude 5.5 models through such a route no longer fail their first call. ([senpi#2957](https://github.com/code-yeongyu/senpi/issues/2957), [senpi#2963](https://github.com/code-yeongyu/senpi/pull/2963))\n\n**Deprecating platform packages for a release that never shipped rechecks the registry before failing**, so a deprecation that is still propagating no longer fails the workflow. ([#9769](https://github.com/code-yeongyu/oh-my-openagent/pull/9769))\n\n- bb9a25534 Merge pull request #9773 from code-yeongyu/docs/5.1.27-notes\n- 64690972b docs(changelog): 5.1.27 release notes\n- 498c508d8 Merge pull request #9771 from code-yeongyu/docs/9770-anthropic-prompt-cache\n- 42a542fa9 docs(configuration): document the Anthropic 1-hour prompt cache and the cache keep-alive\n- 007dbce06 Merge pull request #9769 from code-yeongyu/ci/deprecate-readback-retry\n- fe3db35ec Merge pull request #9750 from code-yeongyu/fix/9749-memory-lock-reclaim-and-backoff\n- 44b16c2b8 ci(npm-deprecate-version): recheck the read-back with backoff for about 2 minutes before failing\n- 2c52bdf40 Merge pull request #9676 from cynkai/fix/9616-ledger-only-for-todo-work\n- 158b64177 Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/dev' into fix/9749-memory-lock-reclaim-and-backoff\n- bb11c1902 Merge pull request #9765 from code-yeongyu/release/v5.1.26-source-state\n- 4cc4939db Merge remote-tracking branch 'origin/dev' into fix/9749-memory-lock-reclaim-and-backoff\n- 69649bc13 test(memory-core): inject the unreadable-lock failure instead of chmod, so the sweep test holds on Windows and as root (#9749 review)\n- 7892ac6b0 refactor(memory-core): split the lock module by responsibility, sweep each dead-owner lock in isolation, and bound the backoff test by its contract (#9749 review)\n- d644aa2da fix(memory-core): read before publishing the recovery lock, back off lock polls with jitter, and reclaim dead-owner locks and candidates (#9749)\n- ea8fec9b5 test(memory-core): lock waits back off, a live recovery holder costs no publishes, and dead-owner locks and candidates are reclaimed (#9749)\n- 2c4009eec fix(prompts): keep the progress-ledger block out of single-turn answers\n\n**Thank you to 1 community contributor:**\n- @cynkai:\n  - fix(prompts): keep the progress-ledger block out of single-turn answers\n\n```bash\nbun add -g omo-ai\n```\n",
